00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:08.019 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Music]  tom clancy was born on april 12 1947 in  baltimore maryland  his father thomas clancy was a mail  carrier for the united states postal  service and his mother catherine clancy  worked in the credit department of the  store  an irish-american family clancy was the  middle child of their family of five  growing up in the northwood neighborhood  in northeast baltimore  clancy attended loyola high school in  towson maryland  after his graduation in 1965 he  furthered his education at the  associated loyola college  while at college clancy joined the army  reserve officers training corps his  lifelong dream however he was ineligible  to serve due to his poor eyesight  but regardless he maintained an interest  in the military and continued to  research various aspects of the armed  forces and military technology  in 1969 he graduated with a bachelor's  degree in english literature  clancy went on to work for an insurance  company in hartford connecticut  in the same year clancy married wanda  thomas king a nursing student who'd  later become an eye surgeon  they would go on to have three daughters  and a son  in 1973 clancy joined the of bowen  agency a small insurance agency based in  maryland that was founded by his wife's  grandfather  in 1980 he purchased the insurance  agency  having always dreamed of writing a novel  this was the time he would begin writing  his debut novel in his spare time  upon the completion of his first novel  called the hunt for red october clancy  sold it for publishing to the naval  institute press for five thousand  dollars  this book introduced the character of  jack ryan  the publisher was impressed with the  work stating that they believed it was a  potential best seller  clancy's initial hopes were that he  would sell 5 000 copies of the book  however far exceeding his expectations  the hunt for red october passed the 45  000 unit mark becoming an instant hit  but it wouldn't end here  later on after receiving it as a  christmas gift president ronald reagan  would praise the novel calling it the  perfect yarn  this would boost the sales to over 300  000 hardcover and 2 million paperback  copies of the book making it a national  bestseller  after the success of the book he became  a sought after name in literary circles  the book was critically praised for its  technical accuracy which in turn led to  clancy meeting several high-ranking  officers in the u.s military  the success of this novel led to his  insurance career taking a back seat as  he focused more on writing  over time clancy became renowned for his  novels that focused on the hero that was  highly skilled disciplined honest  thoroughly professional and would only  lose the call when incompetent  politicians or bureaucrats got in their  way  their unambiguous triumphs over evil  provide symbolic relief from the legacy  of the vietnam war  the next 20 years would see him release  a plethora of written work  which would include stories such as red  storm rising patriot games clear and  present danger without remorse executive  orders  and rainbow six  seventeen of his novels would make it to  the top of the new york times bestseller  list  by 1988 clancy had earned 1.3 million  for the hunt of red october and had  signed a three million dollar contract  for his next three books  in 1992 he sold the north american  rights to without remorse for 14 million  dollars  a record for a single book  in 1995 clancy and his wife wanda  briefly separated  however in 1996 they proceeded to follow  through with wander filing for divorce  in november 1997.  this would become final in january 1999.  six months later clancy married  freelance journalist alexandra marie  luellen who he had known since 1997.  the couple had one daughter together  tom clancy would go on to co-author a  number of memoirs of top generals and  had numerous guided tours of the elite  aspects of the american military  american historian andrew basovich would  later state clancy did for military pop  lit what starbucks did for the  preparation of caffeinated beverages  he launched a sprawling massively  profitable industrial enterprise that  simultaneously serves and cultivates an  insatiable consumer base  whether the item consumed provides much  in terms of nourishment is utterly  beside the point  that it tastes yummy going down more  than suffices to keep customers coming  back  in 1996 after six years of development  clancy would release tom clancy's ssn in  cooperation with virtus studios  a video game based on one of his books  using the same name  the day after its release clancy and  virtus announced the formation of  redstorm entertainment a name derived  from the clancybook redstorm rising  clancy would take the role of chairman  it was reported that by 1997 penguin  putnam incorporated paid clancy and  redstorm for two new books and a  four-year multimedia deal for 97 million  dollars  also in 1997 redstorm released its first  game tom clancy's  political redstorm quickly gained  recognition through games like dominant  species one of the first real-time  strategy games available in the market  but it was rainbow six released in 1998  that would firmly establish the company  in the industry  rainbow six was the first true tactical  shooter where the user was required to  use patience and planning  a complete contrast to other run and gun  shooters available at the time  in august of 2000 while working on the  first game in the ghost recon series  french video game publisher ubisoft  purchased redstorm entertainment  by 2008 ubisoft would also acquire the  use of the tom clancy name to be used in  conjunction with video games and other  multimedia  fox news alert with some very sad news  to report the best-selling author tom  clancy has died  in 2013 following years of heart  complications including a heart attack  and bypass surgery on october 1st tom  clancy died of heart failure at john  hopkins hospital  he was 66 years old leaving behind his  five children and wife alexandra  [Music]  tom clancy's written work has been felt  far beyond the publishing world  some became hollywood blockbusters  starring actors like harrison ford alec  baldwin and ben affleck  some were turned into video games that  were so realistic at the time that the  military licensed them for training  in fact the detail that his books would  go into on soviet submarines weaponry  satellites and fighter planes raised a  number of suspicions and concerns among  u.s military officials  but this was just clancy's style  he spent years researching technical  manuals and interviewing military  experts  the absolute detail was what drove his  novels  critics have since spoken of clancy's  work stating that it was him that was  able to redefine and expand on the genre  allowing many others to publish such  books that were previously unable to  i thought given the amount of time i've  invested into tom clancy's work over the  years including some of his books and  the many video games that have been  inspired by his work it was about time  that i talked about the man himself  i know this video won't be for everyone  in fact this information is something  that i'd compiled together quite some  time ago but i saw it as more of a  personal piece and decided to hold it  back from completion and upload  but as i've been informed recently there  are a number of people who'd like to see  me complete some of these personal  projects and interests so here it is  for those of you who watch this thank  you  while his work may not have been to  everyone's taste it certainly brought  forward a unique flavor to the  industries it touched  thanks again i hope you enjoyed this and  i'll catch in the next one cheers  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  uh

